.TH IRON86 1 "2026-09-11" "iron86 0.23" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iron86 \- chip-level 8086 IBM PC (no DOS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iron86
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIfile.com\fR]
.P
.B iron86
.BI \-\-bios " BIOS.BIN"
[\fB\-\-floppy\-a\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-floppy\-b\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-hdc\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-hdc\-rom\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-keys\fR \fISTRING\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iron86
is a C++23 8086 + IBM PC chip set (PPI, PIT, PIC, DMA, FDC, two 6845s).
It does not implement DOS; FloppyOS or a BIOS INT 19 boot provides that.
.P
.B tdx \-\-bios
embeds iron86.
This binary is the standalone smoke tool.
.P
CLI flags override an INI file, which overrides the preset.
Default preset is
.BR ibm-pc
(5150, floppy only, 8086 prefetch 6).
.B ibm-xt
is 5160: same 8086 plus Xebec (option-ROM scan at C8000).
.B ibm-at
and
.B 8286
(5170 AT, not XT) are reserved (exit 2, "not yet").
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
With no arguments,
.B iron86
prints the same usage.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
INI file. If omitted, load
.B iron86.ini
from the current directory when that file exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " NAME"
.BR ibm-pc / 5150
(default, floppy) or
.BR ibm-xt / 5160
(Xebec).
.B ibm-at
and
.B 8286
print "not yet" on stderr and exit 2.
CPU is 8086 (prefetch 6) on both; pass
.B \-\-prefetch-bytes 4
for a stock 8088 queue.
.TP
.BI \-\-bios " FILE"
8K IBM 5150 at FE000; 40K 5160 concat (U19 8K + U18 32K) at F0000/F8000;
or 64K 5160 (concat U19+U18) at F0000. Reset FFFF:0000.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fast\-post
Cold POST (do not set BDA RESET_FLAG=1234h).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Disable PC speaker BEL (default on).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-8087
Disable 8087 NPX (default on). SW1-2 / EQUIP bit 1 stay clear (DIP 0x2D).
.TP
.B \-\-mda
MDA 80×25 (DIP 0x3D). Default CGA.
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy\-a " PATH"
Drive 0: raw image or host directory packed as FlopFS
(360K if it fits, else 720K 80/2/9).
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy\-b " PATH"
Drive 1: same rules.
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-floppy\-a .
.TP
.BI \-\-hdc " PATH"
Raw HDD image (512-byte sectors) for the IBM XT Fixed Disk Adapter
(Xebec S1410-class) at 320h–323h, IRQ 5, DMA 3.
Must be a regular file — block devices (\fI/dev/sda\fP) are refused.
Default geometry is Type-1 306×4×17 (INI
.B [hdc]
cylinders/heads/spt override).
Writes persist to the host file.
When attached, the IBM 5000059 option ROM is mapped at C8000 if found
(see
.BR \-\-hdc\-rom ).
INT 13h with DL bit 7 set is not stolen (ROS owns C:).
Guest MS-DOS 3.31 FDISK + FORMAT C: + DIR C: work on a Type-1 image.
.B \-\-no\-fast\-post
cold POST reaches A> (10JAN86 SW1 mux is Port B bit 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-hdc\-rom " FILE"
Xebec option ROM at C8000 (55 AA). Default: IBM_XEBEC_5000059_1982.BIN
or
.BR IRON86_XEBEC_ROM .
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Append an event log (HDC/floppy/BIOS/ROS attach lines).
Default off.
Stderr still gets the same lines.
Each line is
.B snprintf
then one
.BR write (2)
(no FILE* log I/O).
With
.B \-\-log
the Xebec ports 320h–323h and 213h are traced to the file only
(IN/OUT handlers instantiated with
.B if constexpr
; the default path has no trace branches).
INT 13h is logged the same way (AH/AL/CHS/DL/ES:BX);
.B DL
bit 7 still returns to the Xebec ROS (not stolen).
.TP
.B \-\-lock\-mem
.BR mlock (2)
guest RAM (1 MiB) and the HDC image after attach.
Default off. Failure prints one line and continues.
.TP
.BI \-\-keys " STRING"
Type STRING as INT 16h keys.
.TP
.B \-\-until\-prompt
Stop at FloppyOS/DOS A> (boot bench; default off).
.TP
.BI \-\-exec\-map " FILE"
1 MiB executed-opcode map.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefetch\-bytes " N"
BIU prefetch queue (default 6 = 8086; 4 = 8088; 0 disables).
Values above 1024 are clamped to 1024 (note on stderr).
Queued bytes are not snooped on data writes (self-modifying code).
A taken jump/call/ret/int/iret flushes the queue.
.SH FLOPPY GEOMETRY
Exact image sizes first, then nearest IBM geometry. No 2.88M on PC/XT/AT.
.P
160K 40/1/8 (163840), 180K 40/1/9 (184320), 320K 40/2/8 (327680),
360K 40/2/9 (368640), 720K 80/2/9 (737280), 1.2M 80/2/15 (1228800),
1.44M 80/2/18 (1474560).
.P
INT 13 AH=08 cylinder count is size/(512×spt×heads).
Directory pack is non-recursive, max 32 8.3 names, 360K or 720K only.
.SH HARD DISK
IBM XT Fixed Disk Adapter (Xebec). DCB sector is 0-based (ROS DEC CL).
LBA = ((cyl × heads) + head) × spt + sector0.
.P
Concatenate 5160 motherboard chips for a 64K
.B \-\-bios
file:
.B cat U19 U18 > xt5160_64k.bin
(1986 32K+32K, or 08NOV82 27256 U19 + U18).
08NOV82 8K U19 + 32K U18 is accepted as 40K.
Prep script:
.B subprojects/iron86/tests/hdc-format-c.sh
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or guest halt), or help/version.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Bad command line, or reserved preset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tdx (1),
.BR tdxview (1)
